# System Call Tracer with Timing Feature

## Overview

This document explains the complete implementation of a **System Call Tracer with Performance Timing** for xv6-RISC-V kernel. The system traces all syscalls made by processes and measures their execution time in kernel ticks.

**Key Features:**
- ✅ Trace all system calls with arguments and return values
- ✅ Measure syscall execution time in ticks (~10ms per tick)
- ✅ Per-process control - enable/disable tracing dynamically
- ✅ Zero overhead when disabled
- ✅ Real-time output showing syscall flow

---

## Architecture Overview

```
User Program (echo, cat, etc.)
        ↓
    Shell (PID 2)
        ↓
  fork() + exec()
        ↓
Syscall Dispatcher (kernel/syscall.c)
        ↓
    Record Timing
        ↓
  Print Trace Output
        ↓
Terminal Output: "PID: syscall_name(...) -> return [N ticks]"
```

