## Core Components

### 1. Process Structure Enhancement (`kernel/proc.h`)

**File:** `kernel/proc.h`

**Added Fields:**
```c
struct proc {
  // ... existing fields ...
  
  // Tracing fields
  int trace_mask;              // Bitmask for which syscalls to trace
  
  // Timing measurement fields
  uint64 syscall_start;        // Start time of current syscall (in ticks)
  uint64 syscall_end;          // End time of current syscall (in ticks)
  uint64 syscall_duration;     // Duration of syscall (in ticks)
  int trace_timing;            // Flag: 1=show timing, 0=don't show timing
};
```

**Purpose:**
- `trace_mask`: Bitmask where each bit represents a syscall number. If bit is set, that syscall is traced.
- `syscall_start/end`: Capture kernel timer (`ticks`) before and after syscall execution
- `syscall_duration`: Calculated difference (in ticks, ~10ms resolution)
- `trace_timing`: Controls whether `[N ticks]` is displayed in output

**Example:**
```c
// When trace_mask = 0x7FFFFFFF (all bits set)
// All syscalls get traced

// When trace_timing = 1
// Output includes: 2: read(fd=0, buf=0x4f1f, count=1) -> 1 [171 ticks]
//                                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^
//                                                      Timing added!
```

