### 4. Process Initialization (`kernel/proc.c`)

**File:** `kernel/proc.c`

**In `allocproc()` function:**
```c
struct proc*
allocproc(void)
{
  struct proc *p;

  for(p = proc; p < &proc[NPROC]; p++) {
    acquire(&p->lock);
    if(p->state == UNUSED) {
      p->pid = nextpid++;
      p->state = EMBRYO;
      
      // Initialize tracing fields
      p->trace_mask = 0;        // No tracing by default
      p->trace_timing = 0;      // Timing disabled by default
      p->syscall_start = 0;
      p->syscall_end = 0;
      p->syscall_duration = 0;
      
      release(&p->lock);
      return p;
    }
    release(&p->lock);
  }
  return 0;
}
```

**In `fork()` function:**
```c
int
fork(void)
{
  // ... fork logic ...
  
  // Copy parent's tracing settings to child
  np->trace_mask = p->trace_mask;
  np->trace_timing = p->trace_timing;
  
  // ... rest of fork ...
}
```

**Purpose:**
- New processes start with tracing disabled (0)
- When a process is forked, it inherits parent's tracing settings
- This allows tracing to follow process creation chains

