## How the Mask Works

**Trace Mask Bitmask Example:**

```
0x7FFFFFFF in binary:
0111 1111 1111 1111 1111 1111 1111 1111
||||                                  |
|||||                                 └─ Bit 0 (SYS_fork = 1)
|||||                                    
||||└─────────────────────────────────── Bit 4 (SYS_read = 5)
||||
||||└─────────────────────────────────── Bit 5 (SYS_kill = 6)
||||
|||└──────────────────────────────────── Bit 15 (SYS_open = 15)
|||
||└───────────────────────────────────── Bit 16 (SYS_write = 16)

If bit N is set: Trace syscall number N
If bit N is clear: Don't trace syscall number N

0x7FFFFFFF = All bits 0-30 set = Trace all syscalls 1-30
```

