## Timing Precision

**Kernel Timer (`ticks`):**
- Incremented by hardware timer interrupt
- Default: ~10ms per tick in xv6
- Measured in `kernel/trap.c` timer handler

**Timing Calculation:**
```c
p->syscall_start = ticks;    // e.g., ticks = 1000
// ... syscall executes ...
p->syscall_end = ticks;      // e.g., ticks = 1001
p->syscall_duration = 1001 - 1000 = 1 tick = ~10ms
```

**Precision Limitations:**
- Minimum measurable: 1 tick (~10ms)
- Very fast syscalls show [0 ticks] but still execute
- Accuracy depends on when timer fires relative to syscall

